experiment: echoname
  SHORT RUN — 100000 ticks against a minimum of 6800000.   ONE creature, both capabilities. imitate reads M1b off a FRESHLY HATCHED
  creature and ctxgrid teaches four-word naming to a DIFFERENT one; no
  individual has ever been asked for both. Reads imitate's echo windows off
  the LIVE session after the lesson, against M1b's own 0.75 bar, with naming
  above its per-creature null as the 4th-rung guard
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  instrument        echoname   trial seed 000000000135cb89   35 teaching trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  INDEX SOURCE 4, inherited from the genome and NOT set by echoname.
  The index reads the AUDITORY module, so a CtxDrive injected into the
  context module is IGNORED by it -- such an arm is DERIVED, not an
  oracle.
  An "oracle" arm is only an oracle when the drive and the index use the
  SAME module: ctx_match reads 1.000 for a genuine host-written index and
  well below it for a derived one.
  the question      ONE creature. Does it both NAME four words
                    conditionally and ECHO which word it just heard?
                    Each half is established on a DIFFERENT creature;
                    no individual has been asked for both.
  the design        two arms differing in one bit -- whether reward
                    arrives. Same index, same CtxDrive, same words in
                    the same order, same number of ticks. The echo is
                    read off the LIVE session after the lesson, so the
                    two halves are the same individual with no snapshot
                    between them.
  the echo          mean held-out accuracy over all SIX pairs of the
                    four words, in imitate's own window (2, 200-600 ms
                    after the word stops, fixed a priori). Pairwise so
                    chance is 0.500 and the bar is M1b's own 0.75.
  the primary       on the taught arm: echo >= 0.75 AND naming above its
                    own per-creature null at 3 SE. The second is the
                    4th-rung guard -- a surviving echo on a creature
                    that learned nothing is not composition.
  the secondary     paired taught - none, as a BOUND with its power.
                    A null is an interesting outcome here, so it is
                    reported as a bound and never as a cleared bar.
  no prediction     the lesson could take the echo (a command
                    overwriting the stimulus) or hand it over (the same
                    heard-word -> vowel mapping the echo reads). Both
                    are results and neither is predicted here.

